"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Three distinct layers (Irish UCITS ETF/ETF share class, as of 6 Nov 2026):**\n\n1. **Transparency-policy disclosure:** The prospectus and website must state the fund's portfolio-transparency policy: what is published, how often, with what lag, and where. This disclosure is required whichever route applies.\n\n2. **Daily public holdings (default):** Full portfolio holdings are published daily on a freely accessible website. This was the historical CBI expectation, including for active ETFs.\n\n3. **Conditional periodic route (CBI Q&A 1012, April 2025):** An ETF may instead publish holdings periodically, such as quarterly with a lag, rather than daily. This is permitted only if the ETF:\n   - provides daily portfolio information to authorised participants and market makers so they can arbitrage effectively,\n   - keeps the secondary-market price close to iNAV/NAV, and\n   - discloses this arrangement and its risks in the prospectus.\n\n**Caveat:** I cannot verify the specific 2026 regulations cited in your bank draft. Confirm their exact provisions and numbering against the published Statutory Instrument and current CBI Q&A text.","ttft_ms":5442,"type":"result","duration_ms":9338,"uuid":"7c574a17-d683-46ad-be18-0286f7b6df56","ttft_stream_ms":1158,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":1158,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
